<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO, SFB - KEY RATIOS.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO, SFB - KEY RATIOS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch ABN AMRO said on</p>
<p>Friday it agreed to buy Standard Federal Bancorporation Inc of</p>
<p>the United States in a deal worth $1.9 billion.</p>
<p>Following is a comparison of certain key ratios:</p>
<p>(All figures relate to year-ending December 1995)</p>
<p>					 ABN AMRO     Standard Federal</p>
<p>    Book Value per Share     Dfl 55.25	    $29.36</p>
<p>    Cost/Income Ratio		67.00		N/A</p>
<p>    Return on Equity (pct)	 13.25	     13.82</p>
<p>    Return on Total Assets (pct)  0.45		0.94</p>
<p>    Earnings per Share	  Dfl 7.69	     $3.7</p>
<p>    Total Income		 Dfl 16.21 billion   $387 million</p>
<p>    Market Capitalisation    Dfl 37.5 billion    $1.8 billion</p>
<p>    Staff			     63,325		N/A</p>
<p>    Total Assets		 Dfl 564.5 billion  $13.28 billion</p>
<p>    Total Liabilities	  Dfl 524.8 billion	N/A </p>
<p>    Shareholder Equity	 Dfl 18.34 billion  $916.3 million</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
